{"Timing race condition in test_basic: background threads may not complete before assertions - the time.sleep(0.1) is insufficient guarantee that the flusher has completed all work, and the test passes inconsistently due to race conditions": 0.7327877283096313, "join() timeout logic breaks early, leaving processes running after timeout - when timeout occurs on any process, the code executes break which exits the entire for-loop instead of moving to the next process, leaving remaining processes running": 0.9534221887588501, "Flusher per-shard buffers never written to; shared buffer never flushed - each flusher process is given a separate, empty per-shard SpansBuffer that is never written to while all actual data sits in the shared buffer that no process ever flushes": 0.9103837609291077, "process_restarts dict never reset after crash recovery, causing false repeated crash detection - the counter is incremented on crash but never reset after recovery, leading to cumulative counting that can trigger MAX_PROCESS_RESTARTS limit even when process is healthy": 0.4357777237892151, "Per-shard SpansBuffer instances share Redis client with inconsistent assigned_shards - operations like record_stored_segments() assert result lengths against assigned_shards, which can yield assertion errors, wrong metrics, or silent data loss when the shard subset mismatches what Redis returns": 0.745162844657898, "Backpressure logic now applies across all processes with OR semantics instead of per-process AND semantics - the refactored code raises MessageRejected if ANY process is in backpressure, meaning a single slow shard will pause all incoming spans": 0.9149824976921082, "Original buffer parameter to __init__ is not stored and becomes unused - the buffer parameter is used only once to extract shard count, then discarded while new buffers are created for each process, creating architectural confusion": 0.813801646232605}